    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="1304" n="1292" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg1292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.4016/10–1545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-15T18:00:00+01:00">October 15, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6050. Dept’s 4613, October 3. Dejean<anchor n="46" xml:id="d628-f1"/> informs me
                    that he hopes shortly to have a definite reply concerning the evacuation of
                    Germans from Austria. He said that immediately after I brought this matter to
                        Bidault’s<anchor n="47" xml:id="d628-f2"/> attention on October 5 telegrams
                    were sent to Generals Koenig and Béthouart<anchor n="48" xml:id="d628-f3"/>
                    requesting their views and asking for an estimate of the number of Germans who
                    would be transferred into the French zone as a result of this evacuation. Koenig
                    and Béthouart are now in Paris and Dejean says this question will be discussed
                    with them “in the next day or two and believes a favorable reply will be
                        forthcoming”.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d628-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 6050, repeated London 755, Moscow 366, Berlin 163, Vienna 22.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For documentation regarding the transfer of German populations from
                        Czechoslovakia as related to the question of the withdrawal of United States
                        military forces from Czechoslovakia, see telegram S–28266, October 17, 1945,
                        from the Commanding General, United States Forces, European Theater, to the
                        Chief of Staff, United States Army, and memorandum by the United States
                        Political Adviser for Germany to the Commanding General, United States
                        Forces, European Theater, dated October 16, 1945, <ref
                            target="frus:frus1945v04/pg_498">volume IV, pages 498</ref> and <ref
                            target="frus:frus1945v04/pg_499">499</ref>, respectively.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d628-f1" n="46" xml:id="d628-f1-content">
                <p>Maurice Dejean, Director General in charge of political affairs in the French
                    Foreign Ministry.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d628-f2" n="47" xml:id="d628-f2-content">
                <p>Georges Bidault, French Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d628-f3" n="48" xml:id="d628-f3-content">
                <p>Général d’Armée Marie Emile Bethouart, Commanding General of French Forces in
                    Austria and French Military Commissioner for Austria.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d628-f4" n="49" xml:id="d628-f4-content">
                <p>Apparently there was no further report from Paris on this subject.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
